[[0,20554,0,9,0,9,"2014-07-22T12:37:00","Tylan","",[],"","Bungie forced to pay $95k to ex-Halo, Destiny composer","http://www.eurogamer.net/articles/2014-07-22-bungie-forced-to-pay-usd95k-to-ex-halo-destiny-composer?utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=socialoomph","gaming"],[1,19589,0,3,0,3,"2014-07-22T12:49:00","Atko","",[],"<p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PSrkfSBiLpg\">Here is the composition</a> (Destiny Main Theme) by this very composer, Martin O'Donnell.</p>"],[1,19590,0,2,0,2,"2014-07-22T13:03:00","bspwmzen","",[],"<p>If you are letting someone, who is prominently responsible for a major part of all nostalgia regarding your most successive games, go without any explanation, then that's a pretty clear sign of PR departement dictatorship over the company. Partnering with (read: Subjecting yourself to servitude to) Activision usually equals letting integrity go and, sooner or later, losing your cause as a game developer.</p>\n<p>It's not like Bungie couldn't have seen this coming, it happened to Infinity Ward before. Also, Activisions CEO is known to be one of the biggest dicks in the gaming industry. Let's hope O'Donnell finds a new place that is more worthy of his talent.</p>"]]
